i focus on easy to understand concept  the food should be just tasty and i  focus on japanese fried chicken because  everybody loves it and everybody  understands it nothing is difficult  about it hi my name is kuniko yagi i'm  the owner chef of pikuniko downtown l.a  today i'm going to show you how to make  golden chicken sandwich and coleslaw key  for this recipe will be being patient  everything had to do with the different  textures pickles has their own vegetable  texture fried chicken should be crispy  but the bun is soft  i made piconico fried chicken as gluten  free because i do have a lot of friends  who is allergic to gluten or the wheat  and i wanted to make a wide range of  customers who can come to pikuniko best  part of  running small restaurants is that i get  to see an actual reaction from every  guest i have that's the best part of  being a chef i'm frying chicken one  piece at the time so that fried chicken  comes out crispy  while i'm using rice flour for the crust  you'll still get the same crunch as  american fried chicken typically  japanese fried chicken has no bones in  so it's easy to eat and also the  marinade that we use is asian  ingredients garlic ginger soy sauce  potato starch i brought my turmeric bun  from my restaurant today but you can  easily substitute with the high quality  hot dog bun and i recommend to toast  them a little bit  new menu inspiration always comes from  local farmers market or the weather but  since we run japanese fried chicken  restaurant i try to make everything  japanese version of something the  favorite part of making this sandwich is  actually assembling there are so many  ingredients and vegetables but once you  get it down it's not too difficult it  may be easy to find like ginger and  garlic and all that but if you don't  have white sesame paste it's equivalent  to tahini paste i'm whisking olive oil  into the other ingredients of sesame  vinaigrette to make it creamy because  sesame paste is full fat i